% This is a placeholder for the parameter estimator Simulink subsystem.
% In a real MATLAB/Simulink environment, this would be a graphical subsystem
% implementing the Recursive Least Squares (RLS) or Extended Kalman Filter (EKF)
% for online ECM parameter identification.

% The subsystem should estimate:
% - ECM parameters: R0 (ohmic resistance), R1 (polarization resistance), C1 (polarization capacitance)
% - Optionally: R2, C2 for 2RC model or diffusion parameters
% - Parameter uncertainties/covariance for adaptive control
%
% Inputs:
% - Measured battery voltage
% - Applied battery current (excitation pulse)
% - Sampling timestamp or sample count
% - Enable/reset signals
% - Forgetting factor (for RLS) or process/measurement noise (for EKF)
%
% Outputs:
% - Estimated parameters [R0_est, R1_est, C1_est]
% - Parameter uncertainties [R0_unc, R1_unc, C1_unc] or covariance matrix
% - Convergence indicator (when uncertainties fall below threshold)
% - Estimation validity flag

% The RLS algorithm implementation:
% theta[k] = theta[k-1] + L[k] * (y[k] - phi[k]' * theta[k-1])
% P[k] = (I - L[k] * phi[k]') * P[k-1] / lambda
% L[k] = P[k-1] * phi[k] / (lambda + phi[k]' * P[k-1] * phi[k])
%
% Where:
% - theta = [R0, R1, C1]' (parameters to estimate)
% - y[k] = measured voltage at time k
% - phi[k] = regressor vector at time k
% - lambda = forgetting factor (0 < lambda <= 1)
% - P[k] = covariance matrix at time k
% - L[k] = gain vector at time k
%
% For ECM voltage model: V = OCV - I*R0 - V1
% where V1 is voltage across RC pair
% Need to formulate regressor that's linear in parameters
%
% With degradation mode awareness:
% - Estimator can be initialized with nominal values adjusted for degradation
% - Uncertainty bounds can be compared against degradation-dependent thresholds
%
% This file represents the intended structure. Actual implementation requires
% using MATLAB Simulink editor to create the graphical subsystem with:
% - MATLAB Function block implementing RLS/EKF equations
% - Delay or memory blocks for maintaining state between samples
% - Math operations for matrix computations
% - Logic blocks for convergence detection
% - Parameter ports for forgetting factor and initial conditions